    reducer-backed mutator), aria roles.
  - `ui/WorkspaceToolbar.tsx` — FR-W3/W4/W5: Import… (`.pcd/.mmd/.mermaid/
    .txt` multi-select), Open ZIP, export .pcd/.mmd/.svg/.png (svg/png off the
    live canvas element; png via OffscreenCanvas guard) + workspace ZIP;
    FR-S2 private toggle; FR-S4 Clear data… entry. Downloads via
    `ui/download.ts` object-URL adapter (zero network — S7-safe).
  - `ui/Banners.tsx` — corrupt-record open error (dismissable), FR-S3 quota
    banner, FR-S2 private badge + 10-minute reminder interval.
  - `ui/ClearDataDialog.tsx` — FR-S4 typed confirm (must type DELETE).
  - `ui/useWorkspace.ts` — hooks: useWorkspace (IDB attach via
    createDefaultStorage → manager.attachStorage (new), init, subscribe →
    version bump, beforeunload/visibilitychange flush, private reminder) and
    useCanvasController (controller creation, active file ⇄ canvas sync,
    palette drop).
  - `ui/App.tsx` — slim shell wiring tree | tabs | palette | canvas |
    properties + chrome; selection/banner helpers as module functions (eslint
    complexity ≤12, max-lines ≤120 per function).
  - Canvas⇄file sync contract (documented for M4): activePath change →
    loadState(manager.canvasState(path)) with loadingRef echo-suppression;
    every ctrl state → saveCanvas (content-compare = no-op when text equal,
    so position-only drags don't write). Two race guards keep init seamless:
    (1) pre-init canvas work is adopted into the freshly bootstrapped empty
    welcome file instead of being wiped by the empty load; (2) when the file
    already mirrors the canvas (autosave raced init), the load is skipped —
    keeps selection + geometry (loadState would deselect). Dirty dot: set by
    saveCanvas, cleared on file apply (open/switch/clear).
  - Evidence: ui+workspace 370/370 (`npm test`); `npm run check` clean; S1
    create-flow e2e + S7 no-network e2e green with the new chrome; 10 new App
    chrome tests (tree render/create/open/rename/duplicate/delete/folder, tab
    close, clear-data dialog, dirty-dot on edit).
